LeetCode 199 — Binary Tree Right Side View

Problem

Given the root of a binary tree, imagine you are standing on the right side of the tree.

Return the values of the nodes that are visible from the right side, ordered from top to bottom.

Example
        1
       / \
      2   3
       \   \
        5   4

Output:

[1, 3, 4]

From the right side, we can see:

Level 0 → 1
Level 1 → 3
Level 2 → 4

Approach 1: Brute Force — Level Order + Store Every Level
Idea

Perform normal BFS.

For every level:

Store all nodes of that level.
After finishing the level, take the last node.
Add it to the answer.

This is conceptually the simplest approach.

Java

class Solution {

    public List<Integer> rightSideView(TreeNode root) {

        List<Integer> ans = new ArrayList<>();

        if (root == null) {
            return ans;
        }

        Queue<TreeNode> q = new LinkedList<>();
        q.add(root);

        while (!q.isEmpty()) {

            List<Integer> level = new ArrayList<>();

            int size = q.size();

            for (int i = 0; i < size; i++) {

                TreeNode curr = q.poll();

                level.add(curr.val);

                if (curr.left != null) {
                    q.add(curr.left);
                }

                if (curr.right != null) {
                    q.add(curr.right);
                }
            }

            // Last node of current level
            ans.add(level.get(level.size() - 1));
        }

        return ans;
    }
}

