We unnecessarily create a List for every level, even though we only need the last node.

Approach 2: Better — BFS + Last Node Directly

We don't actually need:

List<Integer> level

We already know the size of the current level:

int size = q.size();

Therefore, while processing:

i == size - 1

means:

This is the last node of the current level.

So directly add its value to the answer.

